---
title: Dialog
params:
  content:
    description: "the panel's contents: the composing surface's markup"
style: |
  /* Every rule is wrapped in `:where()` — ambient styling is the weakest thing
     in the cascade ([[ui/foundation/button/index.md#^bt-ambient-is-weakest]]),
     so a surface's own dialog class overrides any of this with a plain
     selector. */

  /* The overlay: an element filling the window, centring the panel, dimming
     the screen behind with a flat tint. The strength is a first value to judge
     in staging. */
  :where(.dialog-overlay) {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    /* Over everything, as the spec says ([[ui/foundation/index.md]],
       Layers): the interruption out-paints open panels and every lift. */
    z-index: var(--layer-overlay);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: var(--space-16);
    background: var(--color-overlay);
  }

  /* The dialog format ([[ui/app/dialog/index.md]], Appearance): the question,
     its consequence, and the actions row — left-aligned at a reading width,
     the actions at the end. The composing surface authors the contents; these
     rules are the shared shape they take. */
  :where(.dialog-alert) {
    width: min(384px, 90vw);
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: var(--space-24);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  :where(.dialog-alert h2) {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  :where(.dialog-alert p) {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  :where(.dialog-actions) {
    margin-top: var(--space-16);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }
---
<div class="dialog-overlay">
  <dialog open>
    <div class="dialog-content">{{ content }}</div>
  </dialog>
</div>
